{"version": 2, "width": 120, "height": 32, "timestamp": 1791763182, "env": {"TERM": "dumb"}, "title": "Daemon Doctor demo"}
[0.0054, "o", "Daemon Doctor demo\r\nFake services. No Mac, no relay, and no phone.\r\n\r\nScene 1. Example Desktop App is stuck, then force-restarted.\r\n12:04 UTC  alert: Example Desktop App is open but has no established outbound connection on port 443, so it looks stuck.\r\n12:04 UTC  fix offered: force-restart\r\n12:04 UTC  outcome: Fixed. Example Desktop App looks healthy on recheck.\r\n\r\nScene 2. The network drops. Example Sync comes back. Example Mail does not.\r\n12:05 UTC  alert: The Mac lost its network connection at 12:05 UTC. Other alerts are paused until it is back.\r\n12:05 UTC  fix offered: none\r\n"]
[0.006103, "o", "12:07 UTC  alert: The network is back at 12:07 UTC. 4 of 5 services look healthy. Needs a look: Example Mail.\r\n12:07 UTC  fix offered: none\r\n12:08 UTC  alert: Example Mail has stopped. It is not running.\r\n12:08 UTC  fix offered: restart\r\n12:08 UTC  outcome: Example Mail stays stopped. The demo does not apply a fix.\r\n\r\nScene 3. ExampleTool holds the CPU, then it is stopped.\r\n12:14 UTC  alert: A process that is not on the watched list (ExampleTool) has used 90% of the CPU for 5 minutes.\r\n12:14 UTC  fix offered: stop ExampleTool\r\n12:14 UTC  outcome: Fixed. ExampleTool looks healthy on recheck.\r\n\r\nScene 4. Example Bridge fails three times in one hour.\r\n12:16 UTC  alert: Example Bridge has stopped. It is not running.\r\n12:16 UTC  fix offered: restart\r\n12:17 UTC  note: Example Bridge is running again. No fix was applied.\r\n12:19 UTC  alert: Example Bridge has stopped. It is not running.\r\n12:19 UTC  fix offered: restart\r\n12:20 UTC  note: Example Bridge is running again. No fix was applied.\r\n12:22 UTC  alert: Example Bridge has failed 3 times in the last hour. Automatic fixes are paused.\r\n12:22 UTC  fix offered: none\r\n"]
